    "previous_model_response": "The large triangle has angles \\(45^\\circ\\), \\(30^\\circ\\), and \\(90^\\circ\\), so it is a \\(45^\\circ\\!-\\!45^\\circ\\!-\\!30^\\circ\\) triangle. Since the side of length \\(8\\) is opposite \\(30^\\circ\\), the hypotenuse is\n\n\\[\nAC=2(8)=16.\n\\]\n\nThe other leg is \\(8\\sqrt3\\). Using the area in two ways,\n\n\\[\n\\frac12(8)(8\\sqrt3)=\\frac12(16)x.\n\\]\n\nThus,\n\n\\[\nx=4\\sqrt3.\n\\]\n\n\\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\)"
  },
